# ============================================================================
# WHITELIST-FIRST .gitignore
# ============================================================================
# Ignore everything by default, then un-ignore exactly what is versioned.
# Nothing can end up tracked, staged or pushed that was not explicitly
# re-included here.
#
# This repository is documentation-only: no source tree, no CI, no generated
# artifacts. Adding a new tree therefore needs a `!/dir/` + `!/dir/**` pair.
#
# --- 1. Ignore everything by default ---------------------------------------
*

# --- 2. Whitelist: hand-authored root files -------------------------------
# `.gitignore` must be un-ignored explicitly, otherwise the leading `*`
# stops the rule set from being versioned.
!.gitignore
!LICENSE
!README.md

# --- 3. Never tracked, by design -------------------------------------------
# No un-ignore rule exists for any of these, so the leading `*` keeps them
# out permanently - there is nothing to forget later:
#   .env  .venv/  .idea/  .vscode/  .DS_Store  Thumbs.db
#   keys/  *.pem  *.key       key material
#   *.exe  *.zip  downloads
#
# Verify this file before trusting it:
#   git add -A --dry-run                 lists exactly what would be staged
#   git ls-files -ci --exclude-standard   must be empty
